        "title": "test: prove native command session targeting in QA Lab",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `native-command-session-target` QA scenario linked a harness-heavy Vitest file, so its primary maturity evidence did not prove that a native channel command could interrupt a real active routed conversation through QA Lab.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis replaces the link with a real QA Channel flow. Native command metadata now travels through the QA bus and the shared transport action, QA Channel derives the normal separate slash-command session while retaining the routed conversation as `CommandTargetSessionKey`, and native control commands can bypass an active ordered turn without reordering ordinary inbound messages.\n\nThe deterministic mock provider exposes current in-flight requests so the scenario proves the target turn is active before sending `/stop`. The superseded native-stop E2E case is removed; the unrelated trigger-handling cases remain in a neutrally named suite. No taxonomy or coverage IDs are added.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA maturity evidence now gives honest primary coverage for the existing `channels.native-command-session-target` ID. `channels.native-commands` remains secondary coverage.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qa-channel/src/gateway.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/providers/mock-openai/server.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-catalog.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-planning.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-runtime-flow.test.ts extensions/qa-channel/src/inbound.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/qa-channel-transport.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-flow-runner.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-runtime-api.test.ts`\n  - 9 files, 201 tests passed.\n- `pnpm openclaw qa suite --provider-mode mock-openai --scenario native-command-session-target --concurrency 1 --fast`\n  - Passed with `native command reply=Agent was aborted; recovery reply=QA-NATIVE-STOP-RECOVERY-OK`.\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox `pnpm check:changed`\n  - Provider: `blacksmith-testbox`\n  - ID: `tbx_01kwfm2c2ffg0zm60br2b924gy`\n  - Passed typecheck, lint, import-cycle checks, and repository guards.\n  - Run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28543973404\n- Post-cleanup focused proof: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply.triggers.trigger-handling.e2e.test.ts src/channels/native-command-session-targets.test.ts extensions/qa-channel/src/gateway.test.ts extensions/qa-channel/src/inbound.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/qa-channel-transport.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-flow-runner.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-runtime-api.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-runtime-flow.test.ts`\n  - 8 files, 54 tests passed.\n- Post-cleanup Testbox-through-Crabbox `pnpm check:changed`\n  - Provider: `blacksmith-testbox`\n  - ID: `tbx_01kwfmwqpwxj2gxens8hbjfqk1`\n  - Passed typecheck, lint, import-cycle checks, and repository guards.\n  - Run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28544759562\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --stream-engine-output`\n  - Clean: no accepted/actionable findings.\n\n",
